WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.040
I am about to cross a road,

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:04.120
and here is something you might not know:

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:07.780
In Britain, there are special crossings for horses.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:11.940
Not kidding. Because what I'm on is technically known as a 'bridleway'.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:14.620
It's a footpath that horses and riders can use as well.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:16.620
So here we have a special button--

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:18.620
there's one up there as well

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:19.840
for if you're already mounted on your horse--

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.840
and a special staging area,

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.140
that I'm currently standing in,

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:24.700
in which horses can wait

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:26.460
before the lights change

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.840
and they are able to cross the road that way.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:30.100
And here is the best part:

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.540
the best part is the name,

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:35.280
because in Britain we have Pelican crossings, ""Pedestrian Light Controlled"

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:36.460
they're the normal ones.

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:38.460
And then they came up with Toucan crossings,

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.460
because they were for pedestrians and bikes,

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:42.180
so "two-can" cross there.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:43.780
Then they came up with Puffin crossings--

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:45.480
I can't remember why they're called that--

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.480
but they're the ones with the special cameras and lights,

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:48.460
like those up there--

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:50.460
that will track pedestrians as they cross

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:52.460
and not stop the traffic any more than they have to.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:55.280
And then, because all those are named after flying things:

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:56.640
we have this,

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:59.280
which is a Pegasus crossing.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:03.120
And that is something you might not know.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:08.780
